  - "research before study-playbook" — body has prose then playbook then research then study-playbook, with all four pairs well-formed. Expected reason: `"marker order violation: <!-- aide-research-start --> appeared before <!-- aide-study-playbook-start -->"`.

  These prove that the section-order check (Step 3 in `extractMarkerSections`) treats the new section's required slot (between playbook and research) as load-bearing.

- [x] Update the `3h` describe's nesting cases to add at least one case targeting the new section's containment. Append `"study-playbook pair nested inside playbook pair"` (the spec calls this out by name — "the navigation prose belongs with the playbook" is named as a tempting containment) — body has prose pair, then a playbook opener, then study-playbook pair fully nested inside the playbook span, then playbook closer, then research pair. Expected reason: `"nested marker: <!-- aide-study-playbook-start --> appeared inside the playbook section"`. Optionally also add `"research pair nested inside study-playbook pair"` to cover the next-level containment the spec lists.

- [x] Update the `3j` describe's outside-bytes cases (silently-ignored bytes between sections). The current cases enumerate four gap positions (frontmatter→prose, prose→playbook, playbook→research, after-research) plus a "marker-shaped content outside pairs" edge case. With four sections, there are now FIVE gap positions. Add:
  - `"scratch text between playbook closer and study-playbook opener"` — scratch text in the new gap between sections 2 and 3.
  - `"scratch text between study-playbook closer and research opener"` — scratch text in the new gap between sections 3 and 4 (replacing the old "between playbook closer and research opener" test, which is now invalid because there is no longer a direct adjacency between playbook and research).

  Update the existing "scratch text between playbook closer and research opener" test name and content to reflect that there is now a study-playbook section between them — it becomes the "between playbook and study-playbook" case. Update the "all four gap positions populated simultaneously" case to "all five gap positions populated simultaneously" with scratch text in every gap. Update the assertions in the parameterized `it.each` body to verify `result.studyPlaybook` carries only its own bytes (the helper test asserts `expect(result.studyPlaybook).toBe("\nSome study playbook.\n")` mirroring the existing per-section assertions).

